ports to US\", \"Rare-earth leverage available but risky — would accelerate US decoupling if actually deployed\", \"G20 Osaka meeting (June 29) provides diplomatic off-ramp; both leaders agreed to meet after June 18 phone call\", \"China's soybean retaliation effective but manufacturing retaliation limited — China has held back firepower\", \"US domestic cost rising: 0.3-0.5pp GDP drag from existing tariffs; $300B round would hit US consumers directly\"], \"sources_cited\": [{\"source_type\": \"event_timeline\", \"source_id\": \"entry_2019-05-16\", \"excerpt\": \"US Commerce Department adds Huawei and affiliates to the Entity List. US firms generally barred from selling to Huawei without a license.\"}, {\"source_type\": \"event_timeline\", \"source_id\": \"entry_2019-05-20\", \"excerpt\": \"Google suspends Huawei's access to Android updates / GMS; major US chip suppliers pause sales. Same day: Xi Jinping visits a rare-earth facility in Jiangxi.\"}, {\"source_type\": \"event_timeline\", \"source_id\": \"entry_2019-05-05\", \"excerpt\": \"Trump tweets that negotiations are going 'too slowly' and that China is attempting to 'renegotiate.' Orders List 3 raised from 10% to 25% on May 10 and directs preparation of tariffs on remaining Chinese imports (~$300B).\"}, {\"source_type\": \"event_timeline\", \"source_id\": \"entry_2019-06-18\", \"excerpt\": \"Trump and Xi agree by phone to meet at the G20 in Osaka.\"}, {\"source_type\": \"event_timeline\", \"source_id\": \"entry_2019-05-31\", \"excerpt\": \"China announces it will establish an 'unreliable entity list' targeting foreign firms that cut supplies to Chinese companies for non-commercial reasons.\"}, {\"source_type\": \"web_search\", \"source_id\": \"reuters_pmi_may2019\", \"excerpt\": \"China's factory activity in May slumped into a deeper contraction than markets had expected... Export orders extended their decline for the twelfth straight month with the sub-index pulling back significantly to 46.5.\"}, {\"source_ty